IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: s 173 -- the Registrar's registers of directors, chief executive officers, secretaries and auditors.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Part sgb2. Every top-level name begins with the label of its provision.
--
-- HOW IT READS. The Registrar keeps, for each company, four registers (directors, chief executive officers, secretaries, auditors), in a form the Registrar determines (s 173(1), (2)). Each register must contain
-- the information the subsection lists for the person (s 173(3), (5), (6), (7)); a director's former name is kept for 5 years (s 173(4)). An entry, and a certificate of the Registrar, are prima facie evidence (s 173(8) to (10)).
-- "Director" includes an alternate, a substitute and a local director (s 173(11)). A document is sufficiently served at the address entered in the register (s 173(14), (15)). What the section means for the individual:
-- what must be in the register about them, and where a document sent to them counts as served. The Registrar's own duties are an official's; the row says so and the rule is encoded with no breach path.

§ `Section 173(1) and (2): the Registrar keeps the registers`

DECLARE `s 173 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 173(1) keep a register of the company's directors, chief executive officers, secretaries and auditors (if any)`

DECLARE `s 173(1) kind of register` IS ONE OF
    `s 173(1)(a) the register of directors`
    `s 173(1)(b) the register of chief executive officers`
    `s 173(1)(c) the register of secretaries`
    `s 173(1)(d) the register of auditors`

-- The duty is the Registrar's and has no period: it can be done or not done, never late, so it cannot reach BREACH ("Rules with no breach path" in NOTES.md).
-- src:14761 | 173.—(1) The Registrar must, in respect of each company, keep a
-- src:14762 | register of the company’s —
-- src:14764 | (a) directors;
-- src:14766 | (b) chief executive officers;
-- src:14768 | (c) secretaries; and
-- src:14770 | (d) auditors (if any).
@ref s 173(1) (src:14761-14770)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 173 act`
`s 173(1) the Registrar must keep a register of each company's directors, chief executive officers, secretaries and auditors` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 173(1) keep a register of the company's directors, chief executive officers, secretaries and auditors (if any)`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:14774 | (2) The register under subsection (1) is to be kept in such form as
-- src:14775 | the Registrar may determine.
@ref s 173(2) (src:14774-14775)
GIVEN `the register is kept in the form the Registrar has determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173(2) the register is kept in the form the Registrar may determine` MEANS
    IF `the register is kept in the form the Registrar has determined`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The register under subsection (1) is to be kept in such form as the Registrar may determine" (a bare "must" not done: the provision's own question, fork F-173-1 in NOTES.md)

§ `Section 173(3) to (7): what each register must contain`

DECLARE `s 173 item of information` IS ONE OF
    `s 173 the full name`
    `s 173 any former name`
    `s 173 the residential address`
    `s 173 the contact address`
    `s 173 the nationality`
    `s 173 the identification`
    `s 173 the date of appointment`
    `s 173 the date of cessation of appointment`
    `s 173 an address at which the auditors may be contacted`
    `s 173 some other item`

-- (3): directors: "(a) full name and any former name; (b) residential address; (ba) contact address; (c) nationality; (d) identification; (e) date of appointment; (f) date of cessation of appointment".
-- (5): chief executive officers: the same, with "(a) full name" and no former name.
-- (6): secretaries: "(a) full name; (b) residential address; (ba) contact address; (c) identification; (d) date of appointment; (e) date of cessation of appointment": no nationality.
-- (7): auditors: "(a) full name; (b) an address at which the auditors may be contacted; (c) identification, if any; (d) date of appointment; (e) date of cessation of appointment".
-- "must contain the following information" is a list with no "only": an item not listed for that register answers NOTHING.
-- src:14779 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), the register of a company’s directors
-- src:14780 | must contain the following information in respect of each director of
-- src:14781 | the company:
-- src:14786 | (a) full name and any former name;
-- src:14788 | (b) residential address; [Act 21 of 2024 wef 09/12/2024]
-- src:14789 | (ba) contact address; [Act 21 of 2024 wef 09/12/2024]
-- src:14791 | (c) nationality;
-- src:14793 | (d) identification;
-- src:14795 | (e) date of appointment;
-- src:14797 | (f) date of cessation of appointment.
@ref s 173(3) (src:14779-14797)
-- src:14807 | (5) The register of a company’s chief executive officers must
-- src:14808 | contain the following information in respect of each chief executive
-- src:14809 | officer of the company:
-- src:14811 | (a) full name;
-- src:14813 | (b) residential address; [Act 21 of 2024 wef 09/12/2024]
-- src:14814 | (ba) contact address; [Act 21 of 2024 wef 09/12/2024]
-- src:14816 | (c) nationality;
-- src:14818 | (d) identification;
-- src:14820 | (e) date of appointment;
-- src:14822 | (f) date of cessation of appointment.
@ref s 173(5) (src:14807-14822)
-- src:14826 | (6) The register of a company’s secretaries must contain the
-- src:14827 | following information in respect of each secretary of the company:
-- src:14829 | (a) full name;
-- src:14831 | (b) residential address;
-- src:14838 | (ba) contact address; [Act 21 of 2024 wef 09/12/2024]
-- src:14839 | (c) identification;
-- src:14841 | (d) date of appointment;
-- src:14843 | (e) date of cessation of appointment.
@ref s 173(6) (src:14826-14843)
-- src:14847 | (7) The register of a company’s auditors must contain the following
-- src:14848 | information in respect of each auditor of the company:
-- src:14850 | (a) full name;
-- src:14852 | (b) an address at which the auditors may be contacted;
-- src:14854 | (c) identification, if any;
-- src:14856 | (d) date of appointment;
-- src:14858 | (e) date of cessation of appointment.
@ref s 173(7) (src:14847-14858)
GIVEN register IS A `s 173(1) kind of register`
      item IS A `s 173 item of information`
      `the person has identification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173 the register must contain the item of information for the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER register
    WHEN `s 173(1)(a) the register of directors` THEN
        (CONSIDER item
         WHEN `s 173 the full name` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 173 any former name` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 173 the residential address` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 173 the contact address` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 173 the nationality` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 173 the identification` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 173 the date of appointment` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 173 the date of cessation of appointment` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "must contain the following information in respect of each director" lists the items without "only"
    WHEN `s 173(1)(b) the register of chief executive officers` THEN
        (CONSIDER item
         WHEN `s 173 the full name` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 173 the residential address` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 173 the contact address` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 173 the nationality` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 173 the identification` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 173 the date of appointment` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 173 the date of cessation of appointment` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "must contain the following information in respect of each chief executive officer" lists the items without "only"
    WHEN `s 173(1)(c) the register of secretaries` THEN
        (CONSIDER item
         WHEN `s 173 the full name` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 173 the residential address` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 173 the contact address` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 173 the identification` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 173 the date of appointment` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 173 the date of cessation of appointment` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "must contain the following information in respect of each secretary" lists the items without "only"
    WHEN `s 173(1)(d) the register of auditors` THEN
        (CONSIDER item
         WHEN `s 173 the full name` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 173 an address at which the auditors may be contacted` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 173 the identification` THEN (IF `the person has identification` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(c) identification, if any" limits the item to an auditor who has identification
         WHEN `s 173 the date of appointment` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 173 the date of cessation of appointment` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "must contain the following information in respect of each auditor" lists the items without "only"

-- (4): "The Registrar need only keep any former name of a director in the register of the company for a period of 5 years from the date on which the name was furnished to the Registrar."
-- src:14801 | (4) The Registrar need only keep any former name of a director in
-- src:14802 | the register of the company for a period of 5 years from the date on
-- src:14803 | which the name was furnished to the Registrar.
@ref s 173(4) (src:14801-14803)
GIVEN `the day the former name was furnished to the Registrar` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173(4) the Registrar must keep the former name of the director in the register on the day` MEANS
    IF `the day in question` LESS THAN `the day the former name was furnished to the Registrar`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection counts the 5 years from the day the name was furnished and says nothing of a day before it
    ELSE IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the former name was furnished to the Registrar` `the day in question` 5 Years
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "need only keep any former name ... for a period of 5 years from the date on which the name was furnished" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a); "only" closes it)

§ `Section 173(8) to (11): evidence, certificates and who is a director`

-- src:14862 | (8) An entry in the register of directors, register of chief executive
-- src:14863 | officers, register of secretaries and register of auditors required to be
-- src:14864 | kept by the Registrar under this section, is prima facie evidence of the
-- src:14865 | truth of any matters which are by this Act directed or authorised to be
-- src:14866 | entered or inserted in the respective register.
@ref s 173(8) (src:14862-14866)
GIVEN `the matter is one that this Act directs or authorises to be entered or inserted in the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173(8) the entry in the register is prima facie evidence of the truth of the matter` MEANS
    IF `the matter is one that this Act directs or authorises to be entered or inserted in the register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): an entry "is prima facie evidence of the truth of any matters which are by this Act directed or authorised to be entered or inserted" and the subsection says nothing of any other matter

-- src:14870 | (9) A certificate of the Registrar setting out any of the particulars
-- src:14871 | required to be entered or inserted in the register of directors, register
-- src:14872 | of chief executive officers, register of secretaries or register of
-- src:14873 | auditors required to be kept by the Registrar under this section shall in
-- src:14874 | all courts and before all persons and bodies authorised by law to
-- src:14875 | receive evidence be received as prima facie evidence of the entry of
-- src:14876 | such particulars in the respective register.
@ref s 173(9) (src:14870-14876)
GIVEN `the certificate is a certificate of the Registrar setting out any of the particulars required to be entered or inserted in the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173(9) the certificate is received as prima facie evidence of the entry of the particulars in the register` MEANS
    IF `the certificate is a certificate of the Registrar setting out any of the particulars required to be entered or inserted in the register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A certificate of the Registrar setting out any of the particulars required to be entered or inserted" is received as prima facie evidence of the entry; the subsection says nothing of any other document

-- src:14880 | (10) A certificate of the Registrar stating that, at the time specified
-- src:14881 | in the certificate, a person was named as director, chief executive
-- src:14882 | officer, secretary or auditor of the company in the register of
-- src:14883 | directors, register of chief executive officers, register of secretaries or
-- src:14884 | register of auditors (as the case may be) shall in all courts and before
-- src:14885 | all persons and bodies authorised by law be received as prima facie
-- src:14886 | evidence of the fact, until by a notification of change given to the
-- src:14891 | Registrar it appears that the person has ceased to be or becomes
-- src:14892 | disqualified to act as such a director, chief executive officer, secretary
-- src:14893 | or auditor, as the case may be.
@ref s 173(10) (src:14880-14893)
GIVEN `the certificate states that at the time specified in it a person was named as director, chief executive officer, secretary or auditor of the company in the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears by a notification of change given to the Registrar that the person has ceased to be or becomes disqualified to act as such` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173(10) the certificate is received as prima facie evidence of the fact that the person was named in the register` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the certificate states that at the time specified in it a person was named as director, chief executive officer, secretary or auditor of the company in the register`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "A certificate of the Registrar stating that, at the time specified in the certificate, a person was named as director ... in the register" and says nothing of any other document
    ELSE IF `it appears by a notification of change given to the Registrar that the person has ceased to be or becomes disqualified to act as such`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall ... be received as prima facie evidence of the fact, until by a notification of change given to the Registrar it appears that the person has ceased to be or becomes disqualified" (an "until" once met: the Guide's "In short" line, which lists while, until and except among its plain variants)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 173(11) kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `s 173(11) a director`
    `s 173(11) an alternate`
    `s 173(11) a substitute`
    `s 173(11) a local director`
    `s 173(11) another person`

-- src:14897 | (11) For the purposes of this section, a director includes an
-- src:14898 | alternate, a substitute or a local director.
@ref s 173(11) (src:14897-14898)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 173(11) kind of person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173(11) the person is within the word director in the section` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 173(11) another person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a director includes an alternate, a substitute or a local director" does not say that no other person is a director
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 173(14) and (15): service of documents`

DECLARE `s 173(14) kind of person served` IS ONE OF
    `s 173(14) a director`
    `s 173(14) a chief executive officer`
    `s 173(14) a secretary`
    `s 173(14) another person`

-- (14): "Any document required to be served under this Act on any person who is a director, chief executive officer or secretary is sufficiently served if addressed to the person and left at or sent by post to his or her
-- residential address or contact address (as the case may be) which is entered in the register".
-- src:14906 | (14) Any document required to be served under this Act on any
-- src:14907 | person who is a director, chief executive officer or secretary is
-- src:14908 | sufficiently served if addressed to the person and left at or sent by post
-- src:14909 | to his or her residential address or contact address (as the case may
-- src:14910 | be) which is entered in the register of directors, register of chief
-- src:14911 | executive officers or register of secretaries kept by the Registrar
-- src:14912 | under this section.
@ref s 173(14) (src:14906-14912)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 173(14) kind of person served`
      `the document is addressed to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is left at, or sent by post to, the residential address or contact address (as the case may be) entered in the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173(14) the document is sufficiently served on the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 173(14) another person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on any person who is a director, chief executive officer or secretary" limits the subsection to those persons, with no "only"
    OTHERWISE
        (IF `the document is addressed to the person` AND `the document is left at, or sent by post to, the residential address or contact address (as the case may be) entered in the register`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is sufficiently served if addressed to the person and left at or sent by post to his or her residential address or contact address" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a); service may succeed by another route the subsection does not close, fork F-173-14)

-- src:14918 | (15) Any document required to be served under this Act on a person
-- src:14919 | who is for the time being an auditor of a company is sufficiently
-- src:14920 | served if addressed to the person and left at or sent by post to the
-- src:14921 | address which is entered in the register of auditors kept by the
-- src:14922 | Registrar under this section.
@ref s 173(15) (src:14918-14922)
GIVEN `the person is for the time being an auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is addressed to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is left at, or sent by post to, the address entered in the register of auditors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173(15) the document is sufficiently served on the auditor` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is for the time being an auditor of the company`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on a person who is for the time being an auditor of a company" limits the subsection to an auditor, with no "only"
    ELSE IF `the document is addressed to the person` AND `the document is left at, or sent by post to, the address entered in the register of auditors`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is sufficiently served if addressed to the person and left at or sent by post to the address which is entered in the register of auditors" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a); fork F-173-14)
